 known_facts:
-  - "Generic, prop-driven sidebar with collapsible navigation groups via @radix-ui/react-collapsible. NavGroup[] data drives rendering — no product-specific imports. Products provide nav data; Sidebar handles all rendering including collapse/expand animations."
-  - "brandHref prop enables the brand logo/title to become a navigable link (e.g. back to Core dashboard) — backward-compatible default omits the link. This seam was added specifically for SSO multi-product nav."
-  - "Consumed by core/Layout.tsx (direct import from @noctusai/lib/design-system) and indirectly by all products via createProductLayout(). erp-imobiliario has a dedicated e2e test (sidebar.spec.ts) proving the Sidebar renders correctly in at least one product."
-  - "ICON-RAIL RENDERING (2026-08-27): reads AppShell's SidebarRailContext via useSidebarRail(). When `collapsed` is true it renders icon-only AT md+ ONLY — every collapsed-mode class is md:-prefixed, so the mobile off-canvas drawer is the pre-rail rendering unchanged. Outside an AppShell the context default is not-a-rail, so a standalone <Sidebar> is also unchanged. SidebarProps gained NO new props."
-  - "COLLAPSE TECHNIQUE — labels collapse with `md:max-w-0 md:opacity-0` on an overflow-hidden span, NEVER `hidden`/`sr-only`. Three reasons: max-width is animatable so labels slide+fade on the same 200ms ease-in-out as the rail width (no pop); an opacity:0 element stays in the accessibility tree so the accessible name survives; zero max-width removes the label footprint so md:justify-center + md:gap-0 genuinely centre the icon in the 64px rail. Every interactive row also carries an explicit aria-label, plus a `title` while collapsed which doubles as the icon tooltip a rail needs."
-  - "GROUP-HEADER DECISION — while collapsed, a Radix Collapsible group trigger degrades to a muted icon row (label + chevron collapse to zero width) and the group's open/closed state is left EXACTLY as the user set it; it is deliberately NOT force-closed. Argument: a rail must surface DESTINATIONS, not categories — force-closing would empty the rail of the very icons it exists to show and would make the hover-expanded panel open onto an apparently-empty nav, costing a click on every navigation. Accepted consequence: a CLOSED group contributes only its own group icon to the rail."
-  - "Collapsible.Content drops its indent rail (md:ml-0 md:border-l-0 md:pl-0) while collapsed so item icons stay in the single centred column."
-  - "footerContent is arbitrary product ReactNode, so while collapsed it is CLIPPED (overflow-x-hidden) rather than restructured — Sidebar cannot know its shape. The seed's own BackToCore footer degrades to its ChevronLeft icon."
-  - "Root gained overflow-y-auto: AppShell now pins the aside to the viewport (fixed inset-y-0) at every breakpoint, so a long nav must scroll INSIDE the rail instead of being clipped away."
-  - "Covered by the colocated AppShell.test.tsx (collapsed a11y name + title, max-width-not-display collapse, destinations visible in the collapsed rail, unchanged standalone rendering)."
